@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post, Tag, PostTag]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T18:04:15.892Z }
+---
+
+# Tags on posts
+
+## Context
+
+Readers could not find posts on a topic: the posts list is one feed. Authors
+tag their posts, tags are shown wherever a post is, and `/posts?tag=<name>`
+lists the posts carrying a tag. Topic pages and a tag cloud will read the same
+data, so its names are a contract.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Storage.** `tags` (`id`, unique `name`) and `post_tags` (`post_id`,
+  `tag_id`, one row per tag attached to a post, keyed on the pair). Names are
+  case-sensitive. A tag no post uses stays in `tags`.
+- **Wire shape.** Every post a page receives carries `tags: string[]`, the
+  names sorted by code unit, `[]` without tags. `PostResource` builds it from
+  the `tags` relation, so whoever hands a post to a page loads that relation.
+- **Input.** The form field `tags` is one string of comma-separated names.
+  `parseTagNames()` in `PostValidator.ts` is its only reading — trim, drop
+  empty entries, count a repeated name once — and both the schema and the
+  controller use it, so the limits (5 tags, 30 characters each) apply to what
+  is stored. The field stays a string through validation: codegen renders a
+  field as it travels, and a schema that transformed it into a list would
+  leave the generated contract type disagreeing with the parsed value.
+- **Writes.** `Post.syncTags()` makes the listed names the post's tags, in the
+  same transaction as the post itself. A field left out or empty clears them.
+  Deleting a post detaches its tags explicitly instead of relying on
+  `ON DELETE CASCADE`, which SQLite honours only with foreign keys enabled on
+  the connection.
+- **Filter.** `Post.taggedWith(name)` matches through a subquery on
+  `post_tags`, so the filtered list paginates like the unfiltered one. Page
+  links carry `tag`; a tag link carries no `page`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Invalid tags are refused by the route contract like any other field (422,
+  error on `tags`) before anything is written.
+- Unused tags accumulate. Pruning them is a separate decision, since a tag
+  cloud may want to count them out rather than lose them.
+- `syncTags()` looks a name up before creating it. That is safe on SQLite,
+  where the adapter runs one transaction at a time; on a pooled database two
+  posts introducing the same new tag at once could collide on the unique
+  name, and the insert should become an upsert.
